// os.marco — the OS act surface: the foreign primitives a host fulfills (see
// spec/Hosts.md). Imported by macro programs with `use os.`. Under `--host
// dryrun` these log; under `--host windows` they perform real input; under
// `--host bridge:<exe>` an external program (e.g. AHK) performs them.

the OS is an act.
this exports Key.       // press a key/chord ("e" or "alt+tab"); or a Press set to hold it down
this exports KeyDown.    // press and HOLD a key (released by a later KeyUp)
this exports KeyUp.      // release a held key
this exports Type.      // type a text string
this exports Navigate. // one navigation MEANING: "up"|"down"|"left"|"right"|"confirm"|"back"|"pause"
this exports Click.     // click; input may be a Point to move-then-click
this exports Move.      // move the cursor to a Point
this exports Drag.      // press at (FromX,FromY), glide to (ToX,ToY), release — a real drag
this exports Sleep.     // sleep N milliseconds (a number)
this exports Color.     // read the pixel at a Point; result is a hex text
this exports Focus.     // ok if the active window matches the given text
this exports Repeat.    // press a key on an interval until the frame is canceled
this exports Spam.      // start the background spam loop: { Key|Button, Every }
this exports StopSpam.  // stop the background spam loop
this exports Roll.      // random number in [Min, Max]; result is the number
this exports EightBall. // random Magic 8-Ball answer; result is the text
this exports Name.      // random fantasy name; result is the text
this exports Find.      // resolve an Anchor (Image match, else Colour at X,Y) -> Point
this exports Secret.    // type a stored secret by name (value never in the route)
this exports Activate.  // focus a named app, launching it if not running (e.g. "chrome")
this exports Launch.    // start an app/path/URL via the shell (e.g. "steam://rungameid/...")
this exports Restore.   // return focus to the window that was in front before the last Activate
this exports ClipboardGet.  // read the clipboard; result is { Text, IsText, Empty }
this exports ClipboardSet.  // put text on the clipboard: a text, or a set with Text
this exports MoveWindow.    // move and resize a window: a WindowMove
this exports WindowState.   // maximise / minimise / restore a window: a WindowStateChange

// A screen coordinate, passed to Click / Move / Color.
the Point is a set.
this's X is a number.
this's Y is a number.

// A press-hold-release drag from (FromX,FromY) to (ToX,ToY), passed to Drag.
the Drag is a set.
this's FromX is a number.
this's FromY is a number.
this's ToX is a number.
this's ToY is a number.
this's Button is a text.   // "left" | "right" | "middle" (default left)

// What the clipboard holds, returned by ClipboardGet.
//
// Three states, not two. Through the text format alone an EMPTY clipboard and one
// holding an image both read as an empty Text, and the difference decides whether a
// route may borrow the clipboard: an empty one can be restored, an image cannot be
// saved or reproduced at all. IsText and Empty keep them apart.
the Clipboard is a set.
this's Text is a text.
this's IsText is a boolean.
this's Empty is a boolean.

// A window move: where a window should end up. Passed to MoveWindow.
the WindowMove is a set.
this's Window is a text.   // "hwnd:<handle>"
this's X is a number.
this's Y is a number.
this's W is a number.
this's H is a number.

// A symbolic window state change. Passed to WindowState.
the WindowStateChange is a set.
this's Window is a text.   // "hwnd:<handle>"
this's State is a text.    // "normal" | "maximized" | "minimized"

// A held key press, passed to Key instead of a plain text key. Hold is how many ms
// the key/combo stays down before release — what lets Alt+Tab stay held long enough
// to commit the switch (a fast tap bounces back). Omit Hold for the default linger.
the Press is a set.
this's Key is a text.      // the key or chord, e.g. "alt+tab"
this's Hold is a number.   // ms to hold before release
